WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.267
An earthquake nearly

2
00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.967
four thousand miles away

3
00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:05.900
made waves in this
Nevada desert pool.

4
00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.633
On July twenty-ninth,
twenty twenty-five,

5
00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:12.100
a magnitude eight point
eight quake struck

6
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.100
off Russia’s
Kamchatka Peninsula.

7
00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.700
Twenty-one minutes later,

8
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.600
water in Devils Hole
began sloshing.

9
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:19.967
But seawater hadn’t

10
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:22.033
crossed the ocean
into Nevada.

11
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:25.067
Seismic waves traveled
through the ground.

12
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.767
As the ground moved,

13
00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.133
water already inside
the cave rocked

14
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.267
back and forth—like water
in a shaken bathtub.

15
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.467
That oscillation is called
a seismic seiche,

16
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.567
different from
an ocean tsunami.

17
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:40.400
The waves here were
about ten inches.

18
00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.733
Small, but enough to
disturb a shallow shelf

19
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:44.900
where the endangered

20
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.200
Devils Hole pupfish
feed and spawn.

21
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.333
This event removed
some material

22
00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:50.533
from the shelf.

23
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:53.633
The park described it
as a minor disturbance.

24
00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.100
An isolated-looking pool

25
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.767
can reveal just how

26
00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.700
connected the ground
beneath us really is.
